# Canonical author identity.
#
# The project's commits were authored under three name/email pairs by the same
# person. This maps them onto one, spelled as in CITATION.cff, so `git log`,
# `git shortlog -sne` and anything built on them report a single contributor.
# No commit is rewritten -- the stored author fields are untouched, and every
# SHA stays valid for the published artifact.
#
# Format: <canonical name> <canonical email> [<replaced email>]
# The first line has no replacement address, so it canonicalises the name on
# every commit already using that email.

Sultan Hamad Almogbil <sultan@programmer.net>
